# Line endings are load-bearing in this repository. Two separate reasons.
#
# 1. CHECKSUMS. The READMEs publish MD5s for raw.csv, analysis.csv and the
#    figures, and the whole point is that a stranger can verify them. Git's
#    default on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes every
#    one of those hashes: raw.csv becomes 4c0038e9f569bfe6e199116f6469732d
#    instead of 7b68a001709821c71ece5b8ed209d4d3. A reader following the
#    instructions would get a mismatch and reasonably conclude the data had
#    been altered. -text disables conversion entirely.
#
# 2. THE SHELL SCRIPT. run_all.sh is the one command the README tells people
#    to run. With CRLF it fails immediately:
#      run_all.sh: line 4: set: pipefail\r: invalid option name
#    So it needs an explicit LF rule, not merely the absence of a CRLF rule.
#
# Patterns match at any depth, so win-rate/ and motorcycles/ outputs are
# covered by this root file.

# Checksummed data and figures: never touch the bytes.
*.csv   -text
*.svg   -text

# Scripts and prose: force LF on checkout regardless of platform.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
